Z||000000||Standard||01-03-2000||07:19 AM||||Just got back from Pontiac, MI yesterday.. saw a total of 4 Fieros during the trip.  Real nice black 87/88 coupe/se/formula with aftermarket rims near Madison, WI.  Nice and shiny.  2 red 84/85's going down I-90/94 in Illinois near Chicago, and a White GT Fastback in the silverdome parking lot.  Looked nice, but idled a little rough.  Doesn't seem like too many Fiero's for 1500 miles of driving... oh well, I still had fun!||||reg||14
Z||000001||Harry||01-03-2000||01:47 PM||||During the Christmas Holiday I went from Norfolk VA to Greenville NC - Indianapolis - Columbus OH - Cleveland OH. Durinh this road trip from hell I saw only two Fieros on the road. I was really suprised usually I spot many more than that!||||reg||12
Z||000002||Standard||01-04-2000||04:54 AM||||Sorry to hear that you had the road trip from hell!  I had tons of fun, but I was also with 2 friends who are even more immature than me...  some interesting times, to say the least!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||01-05-2000||12:07 AM||||I just spent two weeks in the frozen wastelands of south central Pennsylvania, and I didn't see a single Fiero from here (coastal Georgia) to there and back.  I was glad to get back to where it's warm so I could pull the sunroof again. ||||reg||9
